// expect-error: reads differently signed and unsigned
// BUG-1018: `u32 x = -4 / -2;` used to compile with ZERO diagnostics and return 0.
//
// Bare integer literals are u32, so the emitter rendered `-(uint32_t)4 / -(uint32_t)2`
// — 0xFFFFFFFC / 0xFFFFFFFE, which is 0 in unsigned division. But `eval_const_expr`
// folds the same tree with SIGNED 64-bit semantics and gets 2, so every compile-time
// decision downstream was made on a value the program never computes.
//
// `const_negative_into_unsigned` was meant to catch this family — its trigger is
// "explicit unary minus, unsigned destination" — but it decides on the FOLDED RESULT,
// and the fold here is +2. The OPERANDS are what get sign-converted, not the result.
//
// Only `/`, `%` and `>>` diverge (the three operators whose result depends on operand
// signedness); `+ - * & | ^ <<` give the same bits either way and stay accepted.
u32 main() {
    u32 x = -4 / -2;      // the author wrote 2; the machine computes 0
    return x;
}
